 the Black Joker. The Red Joker has already been played, and based on card counting (max 3 of any rank unknown), there are no bombs in the opponents\' hands. This makes my Black Joker the absolute highest card (the "Boss").\n\nReason: I should play the ♥K. It is sufficient to beat the ♣Q. By playing the King, I force the opponents to either pass or play a high card (Ace or 2).\n1. If they pass, I play the Black Joker next and win.\n2. If they beat the King with an Ace or 2, I can immediately beat that with the Black Joker (since it is the highest card) and win the game.\nPassing is not an option because if the opponents regain the lead and play a combination other than a single (e.g., a pair), I would not be able to play my single cards and would lose. Playing the Black Joker first also wins, but standard strategy dictates using the lowest effective card to clear the hand.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥K"]}'}
